rage=67%, source=both]\n\nAcute Gastrointestinal Bleeding vs Ruptured Ectopic Pregnancy:\n  Favours first:  black or tarry stool, changes in mental status, chest pain, cool and clammy skin, decreased urine output\n  Favours second: 2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abdominal tenderness, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity\n\nAcute Gastrointestinal Bleeding vs Acute Pancreatitis with Hemorrhage:\n  Favours first:  black or tarry stool, changes in mental status, chest pain, cool and clammy skin, decreased urine output\n  Favours second: 2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity, abnormal epiphyseal ossification\n\nAcute Gastrointestinal Bleeding vs Ruptured Splenic Artery Aneurysm:\n  Favours first:  abdominal pain, black or tarry stool, changes in mental status, chest pain, cool and clammy skin\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal cornea morphology, abnormal cutaneous elastic fiber morphology, abnormal facial shape\n\nAcute Gastrointestinal Bleeding vs Ruptured Hepatic Hemangioma:\n  Favours first:  abdominal pain, black or tarry stool, changes in mental status, chest pain, cool and clammy skin\n  Favours second: abdominal bloating, feeling full after eating only a small amount of food (early satiety), pain in the upper right abdomen\n\nAcute Gastrointestinal Bleeding vs Ruptured Ovarian Cyst:\n  Favours first:  abdominal pain, black or tarry stool, changes in mental status, chest pain, cool and clammy skin\n  Favours second: abdominal bloating, abnormal ovarian morphology, calcified ovarian cyst, changes in bowel movements, dizziness\n\nAcute Gastrointestinal Bleeding vs Ruptured Aortic Aneurysm:\n  Favours first:  abdominal pain, black or tarry stool, changes in mental status, chest pain, cool and clammy skin\n  Favours second: abdominal aortic aneurysm, abnormal aortic morphology, dizziness, feeling of fullness, hoarseness\n\nAcute Gastrointestinal Bleeding vs Acute Arterial Mesenteric Ischemia:\n  Favours first:  abdominal pain, black or tarry stool, changes in mental status, chest pain, cool and clammy skin\n  Favours second: cool skin, gangrene, pallor, paralysis, paresthesia\n\nRuptured Ectopic Pregnancy vs Acute Pancreatitis with Hemorrhage:\n  Favours first:  abdominal tenderness, dizziness, fainting, hypotension, pallor\n  Favours second: fatty stool, fever, jaundice, nausea, rapid shallow breathing\n\nRuptured Ectopic Pregnancy vs Ruptured Splenic Artery Aneurysm:\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abdominal pain, abdominal tenderness, abnormal astrocyte morphology\n  Favours second: abnormal bleeding, abnormal cardiac ventricular function, abnormal cornea morphology, abnormal cutaneous elastic fiber morphology, abnormal facial shape\n\nRuptured Ectopic Pregnancy vs Ruptured Hepatic Hemangioma:\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abdominal pain, abdominal tenderness, abnormal astrocyte morphology\n  Favours second: abdominal bloating, fatigue, feeling full after eating only a small amount of food (early satiety), nausea, pain in the upper right abdomen\n\nRuptured Ectopic Pregnancy vs Ruptured Ovarian Cyst:\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abdominal pain, abdominal tenderness, abnormal astrocyte morphology\n  Favours second: abdominal bloating, abnormal ovarian morphology, calcified ovarian cyst, changes in bowel movements, feeling full too quickly when eating\n\nRuptured Ectopic Pregnancy vs Ruptured Aortic Aneurysm:\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abdominal pain, abdominal tenderness, abnormal astrocyte morphology\n  Favours second: abdominal aortic aneurysm, abnormal aortic morphology, difficulty breathing, feeling of fullness, hoarseness\n\nRuptured Ectopic Pregnancy vs Acute Arterial Mesenteric Ischemia:\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abd